I've stumbled into a few clever tricks over the years.  I know many
experienced players have too.  I'm hoping people will share some of
their more original and clever tricks with the rest of rgrn.

First: TEH RULES
1) the trick must not be commonly known/used.
2) the trick must display original thinking.
3) the originator must be credited (where known).
4) no bug exploits please, kthxbai.

Some Examples (in no particlar order):
1) stumbly's quantum mechanic
2) mrivan's music
3) crassworm's hotel
4) eidolos' Juiblex express
5) cdi's blind teleport

Since none of those are painfully obvious from their descriptions,
I'll explain them in detail.

stumbly's quantum mechanic
----
This requires a pet quantum mechanic, conflict, a magic whistle, and
some form of teleport control.  Your pet acts as an infinite source of
free teleports (no power cost, no hunger cost).

mrivan's music
----
Using a musical instrument (horn/drum) to scare/wake a sleeping or
meditating monster through a wall.  The definitive example involves a
meditating Master Assasin prior to tossing daggers.  Another, less
common, example involves any teleporting liches inside Rodney's zoo if
you have a rubber chicken.

crassworm's hotel
----
>From the Rodney entry: "Four steps to a damage-free hideout: 1. Tame
engulfing monster (doesn't have to be coporeal).  2. Put on ring of
conflict. 3. Get engulfed by your new pet. 4. Remove ring of
conflict."

Eidolos' Juiblex Express
----
A rapid (if dangerous) way to cross a no-teleport level during the
ascension run.  Let yourself be engulfed.  Hit Juiblex until he
teleports to the upstair.  He'll take you with him.

cdi's blind teleport
----
Hit a teleporting monster until he teleports away.  Use telepathy (or
monster detection) to locate where it teleported to.  When it comes
back, it's your turn.  Teleport to the exact square (in empty,
unmapped space), where the baddy ran to.  You will land on the
upstair.

